Purpose and scope
-----------------
TurboHap is available without a licence fee for non-commercial academic
research and teaching. Commercial activities, including paid services
provided by academic or government institutions, require a separate
paid agreement with the Licensor.

"Software" means TurboHap source code, executables, modifications and
accompanying documentation, including both operating modes, to the extent
the Licensor owns or is authorised to license the relevant rights.
Separately licensed components and public-domain material retain their
own terms and status. Naming the Licensor does not transfer copyright
from any author or other rights holder.

"You" means the individual or organisation exercising the permissions
below. An individual acting for an organisation must have authority to
accept these terms for it. Exercising these permissions signifies your
acceptance of the conditions that accompany them.

"Eligible Research User" means a person or organisation undertaking
Non-Commercial Academic Use, including researchers, students and teachers
at universities, non-profit or public research institutions, government
laboratories, and independent researchers acting on their own behalf.

"Non-Commercial Academic Use" means scientific research, scholarship,
academic teaching or training intended to advance knowledge or education,
including testing and improving the Software for those purposes. It
excludes all Commercial Activities defined in section 3. A university,
charity, government agency or non-profit organisation is eligible only
for its qualifying activities, not automatically for all its work.

Ordinary research grants, salaries, stipends, tuition and institutional
overheads do not alone make research commercial. Internal allocation of
computing costs and sharing direct costs within a genuine non-commercial
research collaboration are permitted; purchasing an analytical service
as a customer is not covered by that exception. Describing a service
payment as a grant or collaboration does not change its nature.

Industry funding alone does not determine eligibility. Research remains
eligible only if it is independent non-commercial academic work and
does not provide commissioned commercial deliverables or exclusive or
preferential commercial exploitation rights to a sponsor. Funding
acknowledgement and ordinary access to published findings do not alone
make research commercial.

Publication is not required to qualify. Confidentiality, privacy and
ethical restrictions do not alone disqualify research. Publishing a
commercial project's results does not make that project eligible, and
possible later business benefits from academic findings do not alone
make the original research commercial.

1. Research permission and sharing
----------------------------------
The Licensor grants Eligible Research Users a worldwide, non-exclusive,
royalty-free copyright licence to run, study, reproduce, compile and
modify the Software for Non-Commercial Academic Use.

You may redistribute source or compiled copies, including modified
versions, without charging for the Software or access to it. Copies
must carry this complete licence and the notices required by section 4.
Recipients must receive the Software under these same use restrictions;
you may not broaden permissions in the Licensor's material. These sharing
rights include repository forks, academic archives and direct sharing
between researchers. Recipients receive rights to the Licensor's material
directly under this licence.

2. Acknowledgement in publications
----------------------------------
Publications reporting work performed with the Software must acknowledge
TurboHap and the original FindHap method. Use the references identified
in CITATION.cff and docs/ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS.md for the version used, with a
citation format appropriate to the publication. This requires scholarly
credit, not co-authorship or endorsement. It does not require you to
publish results that would otherwise remain private.

3. Paid commercial permission
-----------------------------
Before undertaking any Commercial Activity with the Software or a modified
version, you must obtain a separate written, paid commercial licence
from Green Neuron Ltd. Contact adrian.carr@greenneuron.ai. Requesting a
quote, downloading the Software or publishing results grants no such
permission.

"Commercial Activities" include:

(a) Providing a customer with imputation, phasing, genetic or genomic
    evaluation, analysis, consultancy, hosted access or another service
    in exchange for payment or other consideration. Charges may be
    bundled in a contract, subscription, membership, levy or wider
    service. The specific academic funding and cost-sharing exceptions
    above remain permitted.

(b) Commercial production, routine business operations, commercial
    breeding programmes and commercial decision support, including
    internal operations where no result is sold separately.

(c) Research, development, testing or evaluation conducted for a business
    to develop, improve or assess its commercial products, services
    or operations.

(d) Contract or sponsored research delivering commissioned commercial
    results or exclusive or preferential commercial exploitation rights
    to a customer or sponsor, whether or not intellectual-property
    ownership is formally transferred.

(e) Selling the Software, charging for access to it, or incorporating
    it into a commercial product or service.

These requirements apply equally to commercial companies, universities,
academic departments, charities, government bodies and their subsidiaries
or service units. Cost recovery, non-profit status, reinvestment in
research and subsequent publication do not exempt paid services.
Outsourcing commercial work to an academic collaborator or public body
does not exempt it either.

An organisation may use the free permission for its qualifying research
and a commercial licence for its other activities. Any use outside the
permissions above needs a separate agreement; it is not silently permitted
because it does not fit an example.

4. Notices and ownership
------------------------
Keep copyright, attribution, licence and public-domain notices with
copies and modifications. Identify changes, their authors and dates;
do not present modified software as an official TurboHap release.

You retain ownership of your contributions, subject to existing rights in
the Software. This licence neither assigns contributions to the Licensor
nor requires publication of private modifications. Commercial relicensing
of contributed code requires appropriate rights from its owner.

Names and logos may be used for truthful identification and required
credit, but this licence grants no branding or endorsement rights.
Rights not expressly granted remain reserved.

5. Patent proceedings
----------------------
If you initiate patent-infringement proceedings alleging that the Software
infringes a patent, including by counterclaim, your permissions under this
licence end when that claim is filed. This applies to such proceedings
against any party. The cure period in section 9 does not apply to this
termination. No general waiver of patents covering independent research
results or your own contributions is required by this licence.

